# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules. Copied into out/ by the build, then the
# deploy script appends the generated RSC payload rewrites below the marker.
#
# 301 is a permanent move. 200 is a rewrite: the browser keeps the URL it asked
# for and the host serves a different file. Cloudflare reads this file top down
# and stops at the first match.

# The two pages the old site had that this one does not.
/order-online     /contact/   301
/order-online/    /contact/   301
/order-online/*   /contact/   301
/appointment      /contact/   301
/appointment/     /contact/   301
/appointment/*    /contact/   301

# The old WordPress sitemap path.
/sitemap_index.xml  /sitemap.xml  301
/wp-sitemap.xml     /sitemap.xml  301

# One canonical host. Cloudflare serves HTTPS and redirects HTTP by default, so
# only the www to apex hop is needed here. If the zone already carries a
# redirect rule for this, remove these two lines rather than keeping both.
https://www.nyframing.com/*  https://nyframing.com/:splat  301!

# --- generated: RSC payload rewrites ---
# The deploy script writes the rules below. Do not edit them by hand.
